    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-calvo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a. (calvus], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make bald, to
				remove the hair</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locum corporis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. A. V. 2, 48, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sampson a muliere decalvatus,</span>”
				<i>shorn</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. adv. Jov. 1, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pueros David decalvavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1
					Par. 19, 4</span></i>
			; 1 Cor. 11, 6.</div>
